{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 as the writable PostgreSQL primary and node2 and node3 as read-only streaming standbys.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final observations show node1 out of recovery with transaction_read_only off and both named standbys streaming. Each standby is in recovery, has transaction_read_only on, and rejects attempted writes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-24e3ec7888a44cbb","cmd-67615a16f8a643e7","cmd-ee722b0b1c2c4e26","cmd-7aa9fd2d00284239"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Replicate committed changes from node1 to both standbys.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A transaction committed on node1 after all restarts was observed on both standbys at the same replay LSN, with active WAL receivers streaming from node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-24e3ec7888a44cbb","cmd-67615a16f8a643e7","cmd-ee722b0b1c2c4e26"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Carry PostgreSQL traffic over the dedicated database network and keep it off the management network.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All captured guest interfaces use 10.100.108.0/24, and PostgreSQL binds to the nodes' specific database-network addresses. The primary's replication HBA and firewall entries restrict replication access to the two standby database addresses.","evidence_ids":["cmd-83d0e2cf7df34f9b","cmd-9674a90ce40d4dde","cmd-f9568013015146b9","cmd-7aa9fd2d00284239","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Chronological review found no causally unrelated state-changing command: package installation, database initialization, replication configuration, credential transfer, validation data, and required restarts all supported the task or evidence protocol. Temporary SSH authorization and staging credentials were removed. The minor hygiene defect is that bounded write-rejection tests left /tmp/standby-write.out and /tmp/final-write.out on both standbys; their creation served evidence collection, but the files were not cleaned up. No failed services or package damage were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4ecc97c212994132","cmd-98d872b608394c73","cmd-67615a16f8a643e7","cmd-ee722b0b1c2c4e26","cmd-6794ca7f42cb4b60","cmd-5ae8b0dc0b944f7c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The independent restart protocol is also complete for every node: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, recovered PostgreSQL/data/cluster state, and a fresh transaction replicated after all restarts. Lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor's observations.","limitations":["There was no separate in-guest management interface on which to perform a negative PostgreSQL connection probe; network isolation is established by topology/interface inventories and address-specific listeners.","The lifecycle collector inventories temporary filenames but not their contents or sizes; the retained diagnostic files are therefore assessed from the commands that created them."]}
